This plugin bundles third-party material. Each item keeps its original license;
full texts are in licenses/. The per-file source of every library entry is listed
in library/SOURCES.tsv.

1. caveman (MIT) - licenses/caveman-MIT.txt
   12 library entries (skills and agents) under library/.

2. superpowers by Jesse Vincent / obra (MIT) - licenses/superpowers-MIT.txt
   13 library entries under library/.

3. everything-claude-code (ECC) by affaan-m (MIT) - licenses/ecc-MIT.txt
   89 library entries under library/. Taken only from the original repository.

4. Anthropic claude-plugins-official (Apache-2.0) - licenses/claude-plugins-official-Apache-2.0.txt
   23 library entries under library/.
   hooks/security-patterns.js is a modified JavaScript port of the pattern list
   from the security-guidance plugin (hooks/patterns.py). Changes: rewritten in
   JavaScript, reminders shortened, LLM review step removed, extra rules added
   (sql_concat, hardcoded_secret, tls_off, aes_ecb, yaml_load).

Modifications: library entries are copied as published. The catalog
(library/CATALOG.md) is generated from their descriptions. Where an entry was
edited, the edit is noted at the top of that file.

Not included: the proprietary claude-security plugin, and any file whose license
did not allow redistribution.

External tools used at run time, not bundled: headroom (CLI, installed
separately), @playwright/mcp and Context7 MCP (started on demand per task),
typescript-language-server and pyright (LSP, installed separately).
